<!-- snippets/jc-buybox-plans.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  "STEP 2 · HOW OFTEN" — the purchase plan rows.

  Deliberately a different shape from the size tiles above: full-width rows with
  a radio dot, a title, a sub-label and a right-aligned price, against a grid of
  centred bordered tiles. The two controls used to look near identical, which
  made eight independent choices read as one list of eight.

  The discount is never a literal. Both the percentage and the per-order delta
  are computed from the selected variant's own selling plan allocation, so a
  plan retuned in Shopify — or priced differently per variant — is reflected
  without touching this file.

  Subscribing applies to the SELECTED size: picking a plan changes jc_price,
  which is the same getter the hero price, the per-can figure, the tile rates
  and the CTA all read. There is no state in which a discounted hero price sits
  beside undiscounted per-can rates.

  Renders nothing on a product with no selling plans — a lone "one-time
  purchase" row under a "how often" heading is not a choice.

  Accepts:
  - id_suffix: {string} Appended to element ids. product__main.liquid renders
      this block twice (mobile pass and desktop right column) and hides one, so
      the two passes must not mint the same id.

  Usage:
    {% render 'jc-buybox-plans', id_suffix: '-m' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture jc_initial_price %}{% render 'jc-initial-price', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
{% if product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0 %}
  <div class="jc-bb-plansblock w-full" style="padding-top:20px;">
    <span class="jc-bb-step">Step 2 &middot; How often</span>

    <div class="jc-bb-plans" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Purchase options">
      {%- comment -%} One-time {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        role="radio"
        class="jc-bb-plan"
        :class="{ 'is-selected': !jc_plan_id }"
        :aria-checked="!jc_plan_id"
        @click="jcSelectPlan(0)"
      >
        <span class="jc-bb-plan__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="jc-bb-plan__body">
          <span class="jc-bb-plan__title">One-time purchase</span>
          <span class="jc-bb-plan__sub">Ships once. No commitment.</span>
        </span>
        <span class="jc-bb-plan__right">
          <span
            class="jc-bb-plan__price"
            x-text="jcMoney(jc_selected_price)"
          >{{ jc_initial_price | plus: 0 | money }}</span>
        </span>
      </button>

      {%- comment -%}
        Subscribe. x-if, not x-show: on a variant with no allocation for the
        chosen plan there is no subscribe price to quote, so the row is absent
        rather than present-and-empty.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <template x-if="jc_has_subscription">
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            role="radio"
            class="jc-bb-plan"
            :class="{ 'is-selected': jc_plan_id }"
            :aria-checked="!!jc_plan_id"
            @click="jcSelectPlan(jc_sub_plan_id)"
          >
            <span class="jc-bb-plan__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="jc-bb-plan__body">
              <span class="jc-bb-plan__title" x-text="`Subscribe &amp; save ${jc_sub_pct}%`"></span>
              <span class="jc-bb-plan__sub" x-text="`${jc_sub_freq_label} &middot; skip or cancel anytime`"></span>
            </span>
            <span class="jc-bb-plan__right">
              <span class="jc-bb-plan__price" x-text="jcMoney(jc_sub_price)"></span>
              <span
                class="jc-bb-plan__delta"
                x-show="jc_sub_delta > 0"
                x-text="`save ${jcMoney(jc_sub_delta)} per order`"
              ></span>
            </span>
          </button>

          {%- comment -%}
            The group offers several delivery frequencies. Showing only the
            first would quietly drop the others, so the rest stay reachable
            here once the row is active. Options come from jc_plans, which is
            built from the live selling plans — no second copy of the label
            derivation to fall out of step.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="jc-bb-plan__freq" x-show="jc_plan_id && jc_plans.length > 1" x-cloak>
            <label class="jc-bb-plan__freq-label" for="jc-freq-{{ section.id }}{{ id_suffix }}">Delivery frequency</label>
            <select
              id="jc-freq-{{ section.id }}{{ id_suffix }}"
              @change="jcSelectPlan(Number($event.target.value))"
            >
              <template x-for="p in jc_plans" :key="p.id">
                <option :value="p.id" x-text="p.label"></option>
              </template>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
      </template>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Keeps the native (no-JS) form POST in step with the rows above. Only
      present when a plan is actually selected — a `selling_plan` field carrying
      0 would be posted as an invalid plan id. The JS path does not rely on this
      at all: jcAddToCart passes the variant and plan straight to addCartItem.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <template x-if="jc_plan_id">
      <input type="hidden" name="selling_plan" :value="jc_plan_id">
    </template>
  </div>
{% endif %}
